Relevant tables / columns and how they will be used  

sales.time_id : join to times so we can isolate Q4‑2019 and Q4‑2020  
times.calendar_quarter_number : filter to quarter 4  
times.calendar_year : filter to 2019 or 2020  
sales.promo_id : exclude rows that correspond to “no promotion” (to be identified)  
sales.amount_sold : dollar value to be aggregated  
sales.quantity_sold : optional aggregation check  
sales.prod_id : for later product ranking  
sales.cust_id : join to customers so we can know each buyer’s city  
customers.cust_city : city name used for the 20 %‑growth test  
customers.country_id : join to countries to keep only U.S. customers  
countries.country_name : identify the “United States …” record  
products.prod_id / products.prod_name : show readable product names in final list  

Typical filter / join conditions that will be needed  

countries.country_name LIKE '%United%'   → keep U.S. rows  
times.calendar_quarter_number = 4  
times.calendar_year IN (2019, 2020)  
sales.promo_id = ?                      → value that means “no promo” (to be discovered)  

